[
  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-66729",
      "knowledge_point_id": "149fa184-850f-52d8-a309-4b79a371a74d",
      "knowledge_point": "Identifying the Intervals on Which a Function is Invertible Given a Description",
      "problem": "Given that $f(x)=|x-1|-2,$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\nI. $x\\in (-\\infty ,1]$\n\nII. $x\\in (1,\\infty )$\n\nIII. $x\\in (-\\infty ,2]$",
      "worked_solution": "The graph of the function $f(x)=|x-1|-2$ can be obtained in the following way:\n\n1\\. Take the curve $y=|x|.$\n\n2\\. Translate it by $1$ units to the right,  to get $y=|x-1|.$\n\n3\\. Finally, translate $y=|x-1|$ by $2$ units down to get $f(x)=|x-1|-2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/assets/753840da17642582f9dbc0debc18f1fa3efcbbb11142894c1dd823ad6c0c630a.png)\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n- The function $f(x)$ is invertible on each of the intervals $x\\in (-\\infty ,1]$ and $x\\in (1,\\infty ).$ On these intervals, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/assets/15f1c797cbddd2ac8e2e9c5be72f842e7d1accfc5f619af57b1f35a27e1015c0.png)\n\n  \n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not invertible on the interval $x\\in (-\\infty ,2].$ On this interval, some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/assets/a100489b49da7b06c98783b1b1c4ec0de9d891fc2b22f4b36b1a0ac2d54fc4f3.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I  and II only\".",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "I only",
