  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069215",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-42728",
      "knowledge_point_id": "d8297713-fb86-59f2-af4d-850af2575541",
      "knowledge_point": "Calculating the Expected Value for a Random Variable with Non-Uniform Probability",
      "problem": "The rolls of an unfair six-sided die follow the probability mass function $f(x)$ as shown in the table below. What is the expected value of one roll of the die?\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3)+4\\cdot f(4)+5\\cdot f(5)+6\\cdot f(6) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{8})+2(\\frac{1}{6})+3(\\frac{1}{6})+4(\\frac{1}{6})+5(\\frac{1}{8})+6(\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}+\\frac{2}{6}+\\frac{3}{6}+\\frac{4}{6}+\\frac{5}{8}+\\frac{6}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}+\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{5}{8}+\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{24}+\\frac{8}{24}+\\frac{12}{24}+\\frac{16}{24}+\\frac{15}{24}+\\frac{36}{24} \\\\  & =\\frac{3+8+12+16+15+36}{24} \\\\  & =\\frac{90}{24} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
