  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069215",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-83642",
      "knowledge_point_id": "8c3fc090-22e5-5f05-9634-b8c645cf5700",
      "knowledge_point": "Calculating the Expected Value Given the Frequency of a Random Variable",
      "problem": "Several children were asked their age. The age of each child (in years) was recorded below. If $X$ is the age of a randomly selected child, what is the expected value of $X?$\n\n| Age | $10$ | $11$ | $12$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Number of Children | $2$ | $4$ | $4$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nWe're given the frequencies of the children's ages, so we can start by computing the corresponding probabilities. The total number of children is $2+4+4=10,$ so the corresponding probabilities are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=10)=f(10) & =\\frac{2}{10}=\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ P(X=11)=f(11) & =\\frac{4}{10}=\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ P(X=12)=f(12) & =\\frac{4}{10}=\\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe organize these results in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $10$ | $11$ | $12$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $\\frac{2}{5}$ | $\\frac{2}{5}$ |\n\nNow, summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =10\\cdot f(10)+11\\cdot f(11)+12\\cdot f(12) \\\\  & =10(\\frac{1}{5})+11(\\frac{2}{5})+12(\\frac{2}{5}) \\\\  & =2+\\frac{22}{5}+\\frac{24}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{5}+\\frac{22}{5}+\\frac{24}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{10+22+24}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{56}{5} \\\\  & =11.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
